# wrangle

- Label: Wrangle
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2048
- Parameters: 10 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/wrangle.html
- Summary (EN): Lets users who know VEX change pixel values in layers through code. It corresponds to the Volume Wrangle SOP but automatically converts incoming layers or VDBs into bound volumes.
- Résumé (FR) : Permet de modifier les valeurs de pixels par du code VEX, en convertissant automatiquement les couches et VDB en volumes liés, au prix d'une exécution CPU plus lente.

- Inputs meaning: ["input1: layers, VDBs or other inputs sent into the wrangle; the page lists only this input, but Number of Inputs can add more; layers and VDBs bind to geometry input 0, so additional geometry uses higher input numbers"]

- Key parameters: ["Volumes to Write to: pattern limiting which layers can be modified; narrowing it speeds up the node because unlisted layers are not copied", "Enforce Prototypes: requires @ bindings (such as @Cd or @ptnum) to be declared first, catching typos", "Evaluation Node Path: where VEX functions such as ch() start their path search", "Export Parameters: pattern stopping the VEX shader from writing to certain volumes; those stay bound for reading", "Rename Wires Using Output Labels: output wire names come from port labels instead of inputs", "Number of Inputs: for each input sets Type (Mono, UV, RGB, RGBA, ID, Geometry or VDB types), Binding Name and Input Index"]

- Caveats: ["Wrangles run on the CPU and can noticeably slow networks", "The page says it is still encouraged to use the OpenCL COP rather than a Wrangle, reserving the Wrangle for tasks needing high-level geometry functions"]

